    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=916806": {
      "title": "Casual Registration Lead - WATLF 2027",
      "description": "Casual Registration Lead - WATLF 2027 Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor Academic Perth, Western Australia Casual 17/10/2026 Casual opportunity | Bentley Campus G05.1 | $54.81 casual hourly rate From December 2026 to February 2027 Job Reference: 1696433 Curtin University is seeking a Casual Registration Lead to support the delivery of the WA Teaching and Learning Forum (WATLF) 2027. Working with the WATLF Project Officer and Teaching Enhancement team, you will coordinate the Forum’s registration operations and support the smooth delivery of attendee administration and on-site registration activities. This is a great opportunity for someone with experience in events, administration or customer-facing operations who enjoys working in a fast-paced and collaborative environment. Key Responsibilities Coordinate attendee registrations and associated administration. Manage registration-related communications and enquiries. Assist with planning and coordinating the on-site registration and check-in process. Coordinate registration staff and volunteers during the Forum. Support event preparation activities in the lead-up to WATLF 2027. Provide general administrative and operational support to the WATLF Project Officer and Teaching Enhancement team. Assist with other event-related activities as required to support the successful delivery of the Forum. SELECTION CRITERIA Previous experience in events, registrations, administration or a customer-facing environment. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. A proactive and flexible approach to work. Strong attention to detail and the ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Confidence engaging with a range of stakeholders, attendees and team members. This opportunity may particularly suit current Curtin staff, Events Management students, recent graduates or alumni with relevant experience in events, registrations or customer service. Hours and availability The successful candidate will be engaged from approximately early December 2026 until 6 February 2027. Hours are expected to be approximately: December: 7.5 hours per week. January to 6 February: approximately 30 hours per week. Hours may fluctuate depending on operational requirements. Applicants must be available during the week leading up to the Forum and for both Forum days on 4 and 5 February 2027. How to apply Please submit your application outlining your relevant experience and suitability for the opportunity. Applications close 2 November 2026 . We look forward to receiving your application. Please note this recruitment process is being used to establish a casual pool only . We will only contact you if a suitable casual opportunity becomes available. If selected for consideration for a vacancy, the hiring manager will contact you directly regarding the opportunity and next steps. Applications close: 8.00pm (AWST), 30 October 2026 About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ Disclaimer: Please note that there is no standardised time for the closing of adverts on the specified date. Therefore, we recommend submitting your application ahead of this deadline. Late applications will not be considered. Inclusion in the casual pool does not guarantee employment, hours of work or an offer of a casual position. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. We reserve the right to remove the advert earlier than the date on the advert. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=916723": {
      "title": "Assistant Accountant",
      "description": "Assistant Accountant Office of Corporate Services Perth, Western Australia Permanent Full Time 17/10/2026 Full-time, continuing (permanent) position | Bentley Campus Generous leave entitlements plus 17% superannuation On-campus amenities including a gym, medical centre, and childcare facilities Job Reference: 1693706 We are seeking a proactive and detail-oriented Assistant Accountant to join our Corporate Finance team. In this role you’ll play a key part in supporting high-quality financial reporting, building strong stakeholder relationships and delivering accurate and timely financial outcomes. About the Role As an Assistant Accountant within our Corporate Finance team, you’ll provide comprehensive support across treasury, investment management, and financial reporting, including cash flow management, investment reporting, student fee revenue, budgeting, financial analysis and statutory reporting, while working collaboratively with a dynamic team of finance professionals. Your responsibilities will include: Support day to day treasury, cash flow and investment management activities Assist in the preparation of quarterly investment reports and investment income estimates and budgets Support the budgeting, estimation and statutory reporting activities Assist in the preparation and analysis on student fee revenue Provide financial advice and detailed analysis as required. Prepare general ledger reconciliations and accounting journals Promote and contribute to a culture of innovation, continuous improvement, and adoption of best practice in financial processes SELECTION CRITERIA You will bring: Demonstrated understating and experiences in the application of accounting principles, concepts and practices Working towards membership of an internationally recognised accounting body (e.g. CA ANZ or CPA) Demonstrated effective verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to communicate accurate information clearly and professionally Demonstrated experience in treasury and investment portfolio management activities Demonstrated ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholders, with the ability to work both autonomously and collaboratively. Demonstrated experience in accounting software systems (e.g., Finance One) and Microsoft Office suite of tools, such as Excel and Word. Demonstrated organisational skills with the ability to prioritise tasks and meet deadlines. Desirable Relevant experience in an aligned commercial organisation or the higher education sector. Role Requirements: As this is a continuing (permanent) role, you will require permanent work rights in Australia to be considered Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2026 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page: https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This full-time, continuing role attracts a salary package of $99,213 - $105,251 (G06) per annum plus 17% superannuation. Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up to date Resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and experience A document addressing the section criteria for the roles (no more than two pages) If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Please note applications will not be accepted via this email address. Applications close: 8:00PM (AWST), Sunday, 25th of October, 2026. Late applications or applications received via email will not be considered, and only successful candidates will be contacted. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. We reserve the right to remove the advert earlier than the date on the advert. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=916382": {
      "title": "Finance Officer",
      "description": "Finance Officer Office of Corporate Services Perth, Western Australia Contract Full Time 15/10/2026 2 x Full time, 6-month fixed term contract | Curtin Bentley Campus Competitive remuneration + 17% super contributions Exciting entry level role for someone looking to pursue a career in finance! Reference Number: 1696409 About the Role: Curtin University is excited to offer two opportunities to join our Financial Operations Transaction Team. We are seeking dedicated and detail-oriented Finance Officers to support the efficient and effective financial operations of the University. In this vital role, you will be at the centre of Curtin’s financial activities, working closely with faculties and business units to provide accurate and timely financial support. Your responsibilities will include overseeing and processing transactional matters, maintaining financial records, and ensuring compliance with University policies and procedures. Your expertise and attention to detail will help ensure that our finance and accounting processes run efficiently, enabling informed decision-making and contributing to the University’s financial health and strategic goals. This G04 fixed term role attracts a remuneration of $79,072 - $83,097 + 17% superannuation and other generous entitlements. Key Responsibilities: Financial Transactions: Accurately process and record financial transactions, including accounts payable, accounts receivable, corporate card acquittals, reimbursement, credit notes, purchase orders and journals in accordance with University policies and relevant legislation. Workflow Monitoring: Oversee electronic workflows related to financial transactions and resolve any issues in areas such as accounts payable, accounts receivable, and fixed assets. Client Support: Provide guidance to faculties and business areas on financial transactions, Financial Systems, and business processes, and promptly resolve queries from clients, staff, and third parties. What We’re Looking For: Qualifications and Experience: Previous experience working in a finance related role. Relevant qualifications in Finance and/or Accounting are desirable. Customer Service Experience: S trong background in customer service with excellent communication and problem-solving skills. Finance Knowledge: Experience and knowledge in finance operations and principles. Computer Literacy: Proficient in Microsoft Suite and financial systems. Adaptability: Quick to learn new systems and processes, with a proactive and adaptable approach to work. Role Requirements: As this is a fixed-term contract, you will require current work rights in Australia that match the tenure of this role. Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction. About Curtin University We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up to date resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and experience If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Please note, late applications or applications received via email will not be considered, and only successful candidates will be contacted. Applications close: 2pm (AWST), Sunday, 25th of October 2026 Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. We reserve the right to remove the advert earlier than the date on the advert. Back to search results"
